// ── Benchmark arena — Cast rules ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// The host runs the IDENTICAL native physics as the other four languages. Only
// these rules run through the Cast interpreter, so the Cast row measures interpreter
// overhead on the scripted portion of a realistic mixed workload.
//
// The host exposes per-creature properties (alive, oob, is_mage, lineage, ancestors,
// cursed) and drives @v:curse:lineage / @v:has_curse for the standing curse.

// Kill every out-of-bounds non-mage creature. (Host's Kill flips alive=false and
// counts the death.)
KillOob::
    @e[oob ? 1] Kill
::

// Apply the curse to a bloodline subtree: tag everyone carrying the offender's
// lineage id. Fired both at curse-time (over the existing subtree) and every tick
// after (to catch descendants born "going forward").
ApplyCurse::
    @e[in ancestors ? @v:curse:lineage] tag['cursed']
::

// The mage's reaction when pushed out: record the standing curse and apply it now.
// (The host has already set @v:curse:lineage to the offender's own lineage id and
// teleported the mage; this raises/refreshes the curse over the subtree.)
MageCursed::
    @v:has_curse = 1 ;
    ApplyCurse
::

// Per-tick standing curse: if a curse is active, re-apply it (newborn descendants).
StandingCurse::
    @v:has_curse ?> ApplyCurse
::
